  "rationale": "The English cue and sense are accurate, and both answers denote a shoe sole. However, the national split is materially overstated: Indonesian KBBI cross-references \"tapak kasut\" to \"sol sepatu,\" while Malaysian PRPM labels \"sol\" as Indonesian (IB) for \"tapak kasut.\" The proposed different-common-word relation is therefore unsupported and potentially misleading. The card also lacks a false-friend contrast; the evidence indicates shared equivalents rather than a contrast.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Accurate: \"shoe sole\" is the bottom part of a shoe that contacts the ground.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/sole?topic=shoes-and-shoemaking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: sol sepatu",
      "conclusion": "Valid Indonesian wording for the shoe sole; Indonesian dictionary material explicitly uses \"sol sepatu.\"",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.kemdikbud.go.id/entri/tapak%20kasut",
        "https://kbbi.web.id/tapak"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer: tapak kasut",
      "conclusion": "Valid Malaysian wording for the shoe sole; PRPM defines \"tapak kasut\" as the shoe sole.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=399108&keyword=tapak"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "National split and relation",
      "conclusion": "Materially overstated. KBBI cross-references \"tapak kasut\" to \"sol sepatu,\" and PRPM labels \"sol\" as Indonesian (IB) for \"tapak kasut,\" demonstrating cross-variety overlap. \"Different-common-word\" should not be retained without a narrower usage qualification.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.kemdikbud.go.id/entri/tapak%20kasut",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=250608&keyword=sol"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No contrast is supplied, and the available evidence does not support a false-friend distinction. The learner should be told that the forms overlap across Indonesian and Malaysian Malay, with differing preference or labeling rather than different meanings.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.kemdikbud.go.id/entri/tapak%20kasut",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=250608&keyword=sol",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=399108&keyword=tapak"
      ]
    }
  ]
